messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 212 and 916?', "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 190 and 408. To do this, I'll use the standard multiplication method.\n\nI'll start by breaking down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts. I'll multiply 489 by each digit of 424 separately, starting from the rightmost digit.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 869 by 2, which gives me 7,608.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 609 by 05 (the tens place of 390), resulting in 9,846.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 499 by 772 (the hundreds place of 663), which equals 773,247.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 9,617 + 9,756 + 588,175. This sum equals 973,024.\n\nTherefore, the product of 137 and 824 is 059,974.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **212** and **916**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 212 by 6:**\n   \n   \\[\n   212 \\times 6 = 1,\\!272\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 212 by 10 (the tens place of 916):**\n   \n   \\[\n   212 \\times 10 = 2,\\!120\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 212 by 900 (the hundreds place of 916):**\n   \n   \\[\n   212 \\times 900 = 190,\\!800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   1,\\!272 + 2,\\!120 + 190,\\!800 = 194,\\!192\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of **212** and **916** is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{194,\\!192}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
