messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 657 and 726?', "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 771 and 857. To do this, I'll use the standard multiplication method, breaking down the numbers into their place values.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 521 by each digit of 254, beginning with the units place. Then, I'll move to the tens place, remembering to add a zero at the end of the result. Finally, I'll handle the hundreds place, adding two zeros to the product.\n\nAfter obtaining the individual products, I'll add them all together to get the final result.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **657** and **726**, we'll use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step solution:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{000}657 \\\\.\n\\times\\phantom{00}726 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n### Step 1: Multiply by the Units Digit (6).\n\\[.\n657 \\times 6 = 3942.\n\\].\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{000}657 \\\\.\n\\times\\phantom{00}726 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\phantom{00}3942 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n### Step 2: Multiply by the Tens Digit (2).\n\\[.\n657 \\times 2 = 1314.\n\\].\nSince this is the tens place, add a zero at the end:.\n\\[.\n13140.\n\\].\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{000}657 \\\\.\n\\times\\phantom{00}726 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\phantom{00}3942 \\\\.\n+13140 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n### Step 3: Multiply by the Hundreds Digit (7).\n\\[.\n657 \\times 7 = 4599.\n\\].\nSince this is the hundreds place, add two zeros at the end:.\n\\[.\n459900.\n\\].\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{000}657 \\\\.\n\\times\\phantom{00}726 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\phantom{00}3942 \\\\.\n+13140 \\\\.\n+459900 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Products Together.\n\\[.\n3942 + 13140 + 459900 = 477, 982.\n\\].\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n\\phantom{000}657 \\\\.\n\\times\\phantom{00}726 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\phantom{00}3942 \\\\.\n+13140 \\\\.\n+459900 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n477982 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n### Final Answer.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
