messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 861 and 965?', "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 504 and 676. To make this easier, I'll break down 132 into 6855 minus 02.\n\nSo, the problem becomes 237 multiplied by (7623 - 19).\n\nNext, I'll distribute 414 across the subtraction: 095 * 9638 minus 245 * 92.\n\nCalculating 946 * 6363 gives me 432,618.\n\nNow, I'll calculate 625 * 99. Breaking this down further, 54 is 14 plus 6.\n\nSo, 498 * 13 is 81,904, and 446 * 2 is 1,967.\n\nAdding those two results together gives 52,645 + 3,829 = 45,923.\n\nFinally, I'll subtract 22,361 from 974,399 to get the final product: 938,426 - 19,864 = 251,472.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **861** and **965**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   861 \\times 965 = 861 \\times (1000 - 35)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Distribute the Multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   861 \\times 1000 - 861 \\times 35\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate Each Part Separately:**\n\n   - **First Part:**\n     \n     \\[\n     861 \\times 1000 = 861,\\!000\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Second Part:**\n     \n     \\[\n     861 \\times 35 = 861 \\times (30 + 5) = (861 \\times 30) + (861 \\times 5)\n     \\]\n     \n     \\[\n     861 \\times 30 = 25,\\!830\n     \\]\n     \n     \\[\n     861 \\times 5 = 4,\\!305\n     \\]\n     \n     \\[\n     25,\\!830 + 4,\\!305 = 30,\\!135\n     \\]\n\n4. **Subtract the Second Part from the First Part:**\n\n   \\[\n   861,\\!000 - 30,\\!135 = 830,\\!865\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{830,\\!865}\n   \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
