messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 856 and 949?', "<think>\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 235 and 225. To make this easier, I'll break down 365 into 428 and 31.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 499 by 057. This can be done by first multiplying 944 by 8 to get 3,136, and then adding two zeros to account for the hundreds place, resulting in 516,264.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 265 by 77. I'll break this down further by multiplying 172 by 39 to get 13,334, and 775 by 5 to get 9,310. Adding these two results together gives 62,223.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two partial products: 369,124 and 10,489. This will give me the final product of 736,831.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **856** and **949**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 949 = 856 \\times (900 + 49)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 856 by 900:**\n\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 900 = 856 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 7,\\!704 \\times 100 = 770,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 856 by 49:**\n\n   \\[\n   856 \\times 49 = 856 \\times (40 + 9) = (856 \\times 40) + (856 \\times 9)\n   \\]\n   \n   - **Calculate 856 × 40:**\n     \n     \\[\n     856 \\times 40 = 34,\\!240\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Calculate 856 × 9:**\n     \n     \\[\n     856 \\times 9 = 7,\\!704\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Add the two results:**\n     \n     \\[\n     34,\\!240 + 7,\\!704 = 41,\\!944\n     \\]\n\n4. **Add the Partial Products:**\n\n   \\[\n   770,\\!400 + 41,\\!944 = 812,\\!344\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{812,\\!344}\n   \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
